[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to Insecure Salt Generation in Password Hashing. This issue arises because the code does not properly generate unique salts for each password before hashing them using PKCS5_PBKDF2_HMAC. Without generating a unique salt for each user, the passwords may be vulnerable to dictionary or rainbow table attacks, where attackers can precompute hashes of common passwords and match them against stored hashes. Proper salt generation is crucial as it ensures that even if two users have the same password, their hashed values will differ, enhancing security.

